<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Waththab ibn Sabiq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 990–1040</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Waththab ibn Sabiq al-Numayri was the founder of the Numayrid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of the Banu Numayr tribe in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diyar-mudar">Diyar Mudar</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-mesopotamia">Upper Mesopotamia</a>. As Hamdanid power faded he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a> around 990, and his tribe went on to hold <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saruj">Saruj</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raqqa">Raqqa</a> and for a time Edessa.</p></div>
